{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Written on the Body"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Alexander Technique"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving Reasons"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use reason clauses to express the reasons for an action, or why a situation is the way it is.<br/>You use words like <span class=\"italic\">because</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in case</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">seeing that</span>  to introduce a reason clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Reason clauses are subordinate to the main clause. They state the reason why things are done, or what makes a situation the way it is.<br/> You can use the following words to introduce a reason clause:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>because</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use<span class=\"italic\"> because</span> to explain the reason why something is the way it is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>since/as</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">since</span> or<span class=\"italic\"> as</span> to introduce a reason that is already known."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>(just) in case</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">in case</span> to talk about things that may possibly happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>seeing that</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use<span class=\"italic\"> seeing that</span> to state that a situation is known."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/>Read the following examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Because she is a computer programmer, Sherri is required to sit at a desk all day long."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since her posture is far from perfect, she was not surprised when she began to notice pain in her neck and shoulders."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She assumed that she would probably have to learn to live with the problem, seeing as she worked long hours and that her job was stressful."}, {"type": "example", "content": "One day, seeing that Sherri was holding her neck stiffly, one of the other programmers asked her what was wrong."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Personal Passive vs Impersonal Passive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the passive voice when you want to put the focus of an action on the object of the action rather than its subject.<br/>You use the Impersonal Passive to report events in a general way."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A passive sentence puts the emphasis on the object of the active sentence. When you use a passive sentence to report an event, the object of the active sentence now becomes the subject and focus of the passive sentence.<br/>You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Sherri was given the pain medication prescription by her doctor.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Passive form to report events in an impersonal way. The subject is not specific, but general.<br/>You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">It is said</span>, <span class=\"italic\">It is reported</span> to introduce the Impersonal Passive form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is said</span> that the Alexander technique was developed by an actor, F.M Alexander. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Alexander technique is said to have been invented by F. M. Alexander (1869-1955). "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Alexander, who was reported to have been an extraordinary Shakespearean actor, tried to find a way to strengthen his voice without conventional medical care."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Alexander is said to have created a teaching method that encourages the body to work more efficiently and holistically."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Alexander technique is not easy, but it is said to be worth the effort."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prescription"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a doctor's written order for medication"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She got a prescription for pain medication from her doctor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about health in the workplace."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pain medication"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a drug used to reduce pain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She took the pain medication because of her sore back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "masseuse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who gives a massage"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She saw a masseuse every week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ache"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pain that is continuous but not necessarily strong"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She visited a good masseuse when the ache in her neck got very bad."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stiffly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a rigid manner"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One day, seeing that Sherri was holding her neck stiffly, one of the other programmers asked her what was wrong."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chronic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "recurring"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sherri told him about her chronic neck and shoulder pain."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "laryngitis"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an infection of the larynx"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After almost losing his voice from laryngitis, Alexander tried to find a way to strengthen his voice without conventional medical care."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lengthen"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make longer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When he learned to reduce neck tension and lengthen his spine, his vocal problem disappeared."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the bones that run down the center of the back; backbone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He found that his spine had become twisted over the years."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "holistically"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to the entire system instead of the individual parts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Alexander is said to have created a teaching method that encourages the body to work more efficiently and holistically."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le02ob03aud10"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and research \u201cThe Alexander Technique.\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a step-by-step guide explaining how to do at least three different exercises. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Using your guide, explain the three exercises to a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research the Alexander Technique."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a step-by-step guide."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the guide to a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about 